LANDING PR for story #753's first step: decision 0089, ACCEPTED, "every readout reads a page of what the writer keeps: one summary row per run, a row per seat, and an index of every event". It is docs only and builds nothing; the build follows in slices.

Operator ruling, 2026-10-19, on draft PR #769, verbatim: "accept all for 0089". Recorded on #753 as: every one of the decision's 15 "Asked of the operator" choices is taken as recommended:
1. three projections, `run_summary`, `seat_summary` and `event_index`;
2. the append carries its caller's fold and writes the folded columns only when that fold stands at the head;
3. triggers keep presence, the head and the event index for every writer, and `DATABASE_SCHEMA` stays 1;
4. integrity at fleet level and in the aggregates by the head check alone, with the full chain check at a run's opening (inspect, the run and seat views, costs, compare), at every verb that acts on a run, and in `brokkr doctor`;
5. every column a page selects bounded, as ruling 2's table has it;
6. the generated `lane` page key and `order_at` (the store-side CASE, a named bend of decision 0071 ruling 7, held by `every_page_is_its_sections`);
7. rows behind their head read first and folded before they are placed;
8. last activity, newest first, within a section;
9. `brokkr runs` lists every run a page at a time in today's JSON, with `--limit`/`--after`, `next` and `VIEW_VERSION` 24;
10. the older runs' count kept, by the index alone;
11. the budgets as proposed;
12. the aggregates' exception (64 groups a figure, medians selected in Brokkr, group counts by `GROUP BY` in SQLite, a named bend of 0071 ruling 7 held by `every_figure_is_its_whole_read`); `graph` waits for a decision of its own;
13. migration by a writer's backfill, a read-only reader falling back to #744's kept read;
14. checkpoint bodies stay inline;
15. slice 1 is the fleet.

Operator's words that framed #753 (2026-10-18, in chat): "yes, draft the summary-table decision, and add pagination to it. Then it can grow as much as it wants, we are still in the milliseconds. Also, 81mb memory for one page TUI is nonesense, don't you think?"; "not to mention 2.5gb+"; "ok, but let me challenge you a bit, think as if you live in 1980s - that TUI is something that could be rendered then. What was the top memory for a machine back then?"; "ok, about that decision, the backend data that with synthesize and design should be usable for the other views as well, so we make all the views blazing fast".

The branch story-753-fleet-summary ends at e9403dfe, cut from main 8bd34fdb, and merges clean with current main. Two files: docs/decisions/0089-every-readout-reads-a-page-of-what-the-writer-keeps.md (new) and its row in docs/decisions/README.md.
- Story run implement-story-753-fleet-one-su-e22349e1 wrote it in three passes (95bc6bbd, b7861c2a, 6a994c21). Its third review returned six mediums, all edits to the decision's text.
- Fix round fix-round-753b-for-story-753-dec-d8a8e2ca answered all eight items in 30057249, 619eed77 and 397d1844. Both runs parked only on the two named bends of decision 0071 ruling 7 (Asked 6 and Asked 12), which the operator has now ruled. The last chief verified every citation itself and found no security residual and no spec defect.
- e9403dfe (controller, signed): on the operator's ruling, the decision's Status reads "accepted — operator ruled 2026-10-19 (PR #769), every choice asked taken as recommended" and its README row's status column reads accepted, with one sentence added to the row: "Accepted 2026-10-19 with every choice asked taken as recommended." No other word moves. Its gates: decisions_index::, doc_truth::, house_prose:: and doc_samples:: (45 passed); typos; ratchet files and clones; git diff --check.
- Carried for slice 4 (named on the PR, not changed here): a LOW, ruling 7's aggregate row reads "behind" runs from their rows while ruling 8 reads a behind run whole, so slice 4 should read behind runs whole in the aggregates too, with one behind row in `every_figure_is_its_whole_read`; and an info, the class-63 range bound `from − 2^63` overflows i64, so clamp it at `i64::MIN`.
- Relation to #744 (decision 0088, open, its landing running in parallel): #744's kept read becomes this decision's fallback (ruling 8). 0088's ruling 5 (checkpoint bodies parsed on the first read) is superseded at fleet level by this decision's ruling 5 now that Asked 4 is accepted. 0088 is not on main, so no pointer pair is possible here; when the second of #744 and #753 lands, the pointer pair (0089 `Supersedes in part: 0088`, 0088 `Superseded in part by: 0089`) is the controller's follow-up, not this landing's.

Every review position, panel member or chief, is READ-ONLY: it changes no tracked file and makes no commit, whatever this text asks below. It reports each finding. Only the implement phase fixes a finding the review returns.

Judge, on HEAD (the base is the merge-base 8bd34fdb):
1. The ruling recorded: the Status line and the README row say what the operator ruled, in the house form (compare 0087's accepted Status on main), and nothing in the decision claims more than the 15 choices taken as recommended. The decision's "Asked of the operator" list reads as the choices the ruling took; no ruling's meaning changed after the ruling.
2. Truth: spot-check at least eight of the decision's file:line citations and measured numbers against HEAD and main (the store's schema and triggers, `section_of`, the fold, the readouts' call sites, decision 0088's kept read on story-744-fleet-refresh where cited). A number the text marks as proposed or to be measured in a slice is not a finding for being unmeasured.
3. Buildable as accepted: each of the 15 rulings, as now law, is specific enough for slice 1 (the fleet) to be commissioned from it: the projection's columns and bounds, the writer's transaction, the triggers, the page key and its index, the budgets and their tests, the fallback. Name any ruling slice 1 cannot be built from without a further operator choice.
4. Form and scope: Built unbuilt (#753); Context / Rulings / Asked of the operator / Consequences; the index row's status agrees with the header (decisions_index); only the two files; no edit to another decision's text; no jscpd clone.
5. For the PR: the operator has ruled; name any further ruling this landing finds needed, or say none.

This run lands one pull request under decision 0051, so the contribution gate can vouch for it.

For the implement phase only: if a finding returns the branch, fix exactly that finding in the decision text, without changing the meaning of any ruling the operator accepted. Then run, all clean: cargo test -p brokkr-cli --test it --locked -- decisions_index:: doc_truth:: house_prose:: doc_samples::; typos --hidden; quality/ratchet.sh files and clones; git diff --check.

Other work runs in parallel. Decision 0065 slice two (the-forge-b9; NEVER message it, or any brokkr-wt-* seat) runs U8a2b on brokkr-runtime engine/broker* and engine.rs. #744 (decision 0088) lands brokkr-cli fleet/, tui/ and tui_read.rs. #735 edits brokkr-cli recipes/ and decision 0083. #288 slices L and M edit brokkr-runtime agents/ and bundle/compose.rs. #349 slice 8 edits brokkr-runtime dispatch sites. This landing touches none of their files.

Commit one signed-off commit ending "Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>" if a fix is needed, and never push. Do not run scripts/coverage-exact.sh; the controller runs it. Run every command in the foreground: never background a command or schedule a wakeup, because a headless seat ends when it waits.

Threat model (operator ruling, 2026-09-26): catch realistic accidental misuse, and fail closed on what cannot be read.
